---
title: Greek chicken kebabs
servings: 6
tags: [greek, chicken, grill, summer]
cuisine: greek
time: 45 minutes, plus 4 hours marinating
source: Souvlaki (Best Chicken Souvlaki Recipe) by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/souvlaki.html
---

== Chicken ==

Pound the @boneless skinless chicken breasts{2%lb}(or tenderloins) in a
#zip-top bag{} to an even 1/2 inch. Tenderloins can skip this. Cut into 2-inch
chunks.

In a large bowl, whisk the @extra virgin olive oil{6%tbsp},
@garlic{4%cloves}(large, minced), @dried oregano{2%tsp}, @honey{1%tsp},
@salt{1 1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and
@lemon zest{1%tbsp}(from 1 large lemon). Stir in the chicken, cover, and
refrigerate at least ~{4%hours}, or overnight.

Thread the chicken onto about six #skewers{}, folding any long thin strips over
on themselves. Leave a little space between pieces.

> Soak wooden skewers in water for 30 minutes first so they don't burn.

Heat the #grill{} to medium-high and wipe the grate with a paper towel dipped
in @vegetable oil{}. Grill the skewers covered, turning so they colour evenly,
~{5%minutes} to ~{7%minutes} in all, until cooked through. Cover them on a
platter while you warm the @pita bread{} on the grill.

== Tzatziki ==

Grate the @cucumber{1}(English, seeded) coarsely and squeeze it as dry as you
can; you want about a cup.

Mix it with the @Greek yogurt{1 1/2%cup}(plain, 2% or whole milk),
@garlic{2%cloves}(small, minced), @extra virgin olive oil{2%tbsp}, a scant
@salt{3/4%tsp}, @black pepper{1/4%tsp} and
@fresh dill{2%tbsp}(or mint, finely chopped). Taste and adjust. It keeps two days in the fridge.

Serve the skewers with the tzatziki, warm pita and @lemon{}(wedges).

> No grill: use a grill pan over medium-high, 3 to 4 minutes a side, or broil on high 5 to 6 inches from the element, 3 to 4 minutes a side.
